      "raw_mention": "$XLE",
      "text": "@Yeah_Dave I don't do your hold for dear life strategy with a few individual stocks and hedge along the way. \n\nI personally hedge by shifting portfolio concentration by doing sector rotation. \n\nFor example Iran/US tensions $CVX / $XLE and likely defense goes up, trim other weightings. These are natural hedges rather than puts, and as long as more things go green then red, it's effective. \n\nPost-greenland peace deal for example -> trim $OSS and related sector correlation to military. \n\nPost Google capex -> up exposure to semi trade/photonics BOM. \n\nI think you focus more on small cap like $TE, $QS where my portfolio is split between semi supply chain bottlenecks + energy.  \n\nStrategy would probably be a lot different, mine is extremely active management based on macro catalysts, supply chain mapping, and earning forecasts.",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2024774175890756062",
      "kind": "reply",
      "engagement": {
